# Web quality standards

When editing pages, components, styles, tokens, hero/media, marketing copy, or anything affecting Lighthouse, SEO, or accessibility, read and follow the project skill:

`.cursor/skills/web-quality-standards/SKILL.md`

**Keep the skill current:** when fixing a new audit/quality finding, update that skill (and this short list if it is a non-negotiable) in the same PR.

Non-negotiables (details in the skill):

- Keep brand coral at `#c0392b` (or deeper) so text/eyebrows pass WCAG AA on cream and white — never restore `#f26b5e` for those uses.
- No bare repeated “Learn more” / “Saber más” link text; include the destination topic in the anchor.
- Homepage LCP must be the prioritized hero `<img>` (`fetchpriority="high"`, not lazy). Do not use `video[poster]` over that image. Preload the same format `<picture>` selects (AVIF today).
- Zaraz `/cdn-cgi/zaraz/s.js` needs a browser `Cache-Control` via a Cloudflare Response Header Transform (not `public/_headers`). Zone `41a145bf2688a227f9e321a31055fe19` is in deploy; see README / `npm run cf:zaraz-cache`.
- Blog posts ship full EN + ES bodies (`src/content/blog/<slug>.md` and `src/content/blog/es/<slug>.md`) — never English-only content under `/es/blog/`.
- Non-essential cookies/trackers (analytics) require prior consent — do not load them before Accept; keep Consent Mode defaults denied.
- Canonical URLs use trailing slashes; `/privacy`, `/es/privacy`, `/accessibility`, `/es/accessibility`, `/terms`, `/es/terms`, contact/assessment/blog/services/industries (EN+ES), and legacy `.html` URLs must 301 (not 307) to the slashed forms. Sitemap hreflang must include `x-default`. ES blog index title must be localized (not identical to EN).
- Legacy WordPress leftovers: 301 `/home/`, `/under-construction/`, `/comments/feed/` in `public/_redirects`; 301 `/?page_id=` / `/?p=` via the Worker wrapper (`scripts/wrap-worker-wp-query.mjs`) — do not 200 the homepage at those query URLs. `/phone-systems/` 301s to `/services/managed-it/` (not a live page).
- Marketing copy: industry-page specificity is the voice model — no service-overview SEO-echo third paragraphs; no “theater/teatro / slide deck / not another demo” denial stack; engineer-reply trust line once per surface. ES is Colombian Spanish per skill glossary (`roadmap` → plan estratégico; `scorecard`/`guardrails`/`backup` context maps; `headcount` → planta de personal; `P&L` → P&G; `shadow AI` → uso no autorizado… / IA en la sombra; `deck` → presentación; `warehouse` → bodega; `tabletop` → ejercicio de simulación de mesa; etc. — full table in the skill).
- Lead delivery (`src/lib/lead-delivery.ts`) must never return `ok` in production without a configured sink (Attio or Web3Forms) — console-only success is dev-only.
- Founder-career case studies use `storyAttribution: 'founder-leadership'` and never claim Cybercon customer delivery.
- Homepage leads with managed IT/cybersecurity as pillars, not a flat ten-item services grid above the fold.
- Assessment/CTA copy must not promise an instant cost calculator unless one ships with the CTA.
- LocalBusiness schema: mailing PMB address carries a "no customer visits" description; `areaServed` is the service area, not the mailing city.
- Public `GET /api/health` stays minimal (`{ ok, time }`); detailed dependency status is at `/api/health/detail`, gated by `HEALTH_DETAIL_TOKEN`.
- `/client` and `/es/client` fail closed (503) without Auth0 configured — never a fake login or auth-skipped client area. Auth0 login/callback/logout stay on English `/client/*` routes.